WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:04.444
Unit twenty-three. Intellectual Property in Tech!

2
00:00:05.409 --> 00:00:09.885
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.935 --> 00:00:13.835
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.885 --> 00:00:18.380
Today we learn about Intellectual Property in Tech. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.206 --> 00:00:24.000
Intellectual property. Say it with me. Intellectual property!

6
00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:31.110
Copyright. Say it with me. Copyright!

7
00:00:34.666 --> 00:00:38.125
Patent. Say it with me. Patent!

8
00:00:41.569 --> 00:00:45.388
Trademark. Say it with me. Trademark!

9
00:00:48.913 --> 00:00:52.871
License. Say it with me. License!

10
00:00:56.397 --> 00:01:00.855
Open source. Say it with me. Open source!

11
00:01:04.307 --> 00:01:07.440
Code. Say it with me. Code!

12
00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:14.681
Rights. Say it with me. Rights!

13
00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:32.466
Intellectual property protects creations. Copyright protects code and content, a patent protects inventions, and a trademark protects brand names. Every software license, including open source, sets rights and rules.

14
00:01:32.516 --> 00:01:36.038
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.908
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.108
Patent!

17
00:01:43.942 --> 00:01:49.281
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:49.331 --> 00:01:50.481
Code!

19
00:01:51.327 --> 00:01:58.165
Did you know? Open source licences give permission to use code, but many still have conditions to follow!

20
00:01:58.215 --> 00:02:00.497
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:10.190
Think and answer. What is the difference between a patent and copyright?

22
00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.390
Great answer!

23
00:02:12.568 --> 00:02:17.604
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:17.654 --> 00:02:20.643
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

